# C# .NET Standards

- Follow .NET naming: PascalCase for public members, `_camelCase` for private fields
{{#if parameters.nullableReferenceTypes}}
- Enable nullable reference types; annotate APIs with `?` and guard nulls at boundaries
{{/if}}
{{#if parameters.minimalApis}}
- Group minimal API endpoints by feature; use endpoint filters for cross-cutting concerns
{{else}}
- Use controller-based APIs with thin controllers; business logic in application services
{{/if}}
{{#if parameters.asyncAllTheWay}}
- Use `async`/`await` end-to-end; suffix async methods with `Async`
- Avoid `.Result` and `.Wait()` on tasks
{{/if}}
- Use `IOptions<T>` for configuration; validate options at startup
- Unit test with xUnit; integration tests with `WebApplicationFactory`
